{"user": "So if white is in a corner I could block it in and have it flipped?", "user_ts": "2026-08-04T13:29:15.415840+00:00", "assistant": "No \u2014 a disc **in a corner can never be flipped**.\n\nTo flip a disc, you must trap it **between two of your discs** in a straight line. But a corner has no square \u201cbehind\u201d it, so it can\u2019t be surrounded from both ends.\n\nSo if White owns a corner, it is **permanent White**. You can only try to limit the damage by controlling nearby edge squares, but you can\u2019t flip the corner itself.\n\nAlso in this position the board is full, so the game is already over.", "assistant_started_ts": "2026-08-04T13:29:17.938101+00:00", "assistant_ts": "2026-08-04T13:29:19.684105+00:00", "annotation_user": {"final": ["Common Ground Question"], "consensus": ["Common Ground Question"], "votes": {"Think Aloud": 1, "Common Ground Question": 3}, "confidence": {"Think Aloud": 0.3333333333333333, "Common Ground Question": 1.0}, "per_model": {"llama": ["Think Aloud", "Common Ground Question"], "sonnet": ["Common Ground Question"], "gpt": ["Common Ground Question"]}, "n_valid": 3, "min_votes": 2, "no_majority": false, "needs_review": false, "arbiter_used": false}, "annotation_assistant": {"final": ["Direct Instruction", "Negative Feedback"], "consensus": ["Direct Instruction", "Negative Feedback"], "votes": {"Direct Instruction": 3, "Negative Feedback": 3}, "confidence": {"Direct Instruction": 1.0, "Negative Feedback": 1.0}, "per_model": {"gpt": ["Direct Instruction", "Negative Feedback"], "llama": ["Direct Instruction", "Negative Feedback"], "sonnet": ["Direct Instruction", "Negative Feedback"]}, "n_valid": 3, "min_votes": 2, "no_majority": false, "needs_review": false, "arbiter_used": false}, "annotation_assistant_fine": {"final": ["Board Report", "Local Justification", "General Principle", "Negative Feedback"], "consensus": ["Board Report", "Local Justification", "General Principle", "Negative Feedback"], "votes": {"Board Report":